  info: memory-side cache (node 0 index 1 17179869184 bytes direct-mapped; node 1 index 1 17179869184 bytes direct-mapped; node 2 index 1 17179869184 bytes direct-mapped; node 3 index 1 17179869184 bytes direct-mapped) — HBM cache mode on Xeon CPU Max, or another 2LM memory; pods need no change
  info: Intel suggests page_alloc.shuffle=y on the kernel cmdline to even out conflict misses; needs CONFIG_SHUFFLE_PAGE_ALLOCATOR=y. Check as root: sudo cat /sys/module/page_alloc/parameters/shuffle (Y = on). Apply: sudo grubby --update-kernel=ALL --args=page_alloc.shuffle=y (Fedora/RHEL), or add it to GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT in /etc/default/grub then sudo update-grub (Debian/Ubuntu) or sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg; reboot. Revert: sudo grubby --update-kernel=ALL --remove-args=page_alloc.shuffle, or remove it from /etc/default/grub and rerun the same command; reboot
  info: RDT allocation (rdt_a: cat_l3 cdp_l3 mba) — resctrl classes are available but left off: the balloons policy ships control.rdt.enable: false because enabling it rewrites the host's /sys/fs/resctrl. To opt in, mount resctrl on the host (mount -t resctrl resctrl /sys/fs/resctrl) and set control.rdt.enable: true in nri-balloons.yml; usePodQoSAsDefaultClass then gives BestEffort/Burstable/Guaranteed pods 33%/66%/100% of the L3
